REASON U3_p: an exact cubic in t, the (P) form; the consumer evaluates it at its t
REASON R_cross and R_ins: t^m (m >= 4) times J-free integrals on group D's measure, which majorizes the plain one: nondecreasing in t
REASON R_main: ((N-1)/2) U's R_E + rho4 (nonincreasing in J by U's reasons) plus alpha1 times the U chain on Q - 2 delta B_Y and Q - 2 T(t) - 2 delta B_Y, with hbar_j at t = 1/300 (majorizing every t' <= t) and the matrices Loewner-decreasing in t (the t-part of T is PSD, delta B_Y is J-free): nondecreasing in t
REASON tail: t-powers times J-free norms, times U's Chernoff sum (nonincreasing in J by U's reasons)
REASON off-Omega: ((N-1)/2 + J/2) times U's annulus, far and equator J-bounds, nonincreasing for J >= 300 by C-FAR-H
REASON PR: PR = pref_arb(N), a ratio of reduced Laplacian determinants of fixed strip graphs, does not depend on J
REASON TW: every TW error sits inside the certified J = 300 enclosures; each reason compares exact J-bounds with the exact J = 300 bound, which the enclosure upper end majorizes
REASON Z4: each J-bound is the chain at its own Omega(J) and tilt T(1/J) before the comparison, so the comparison is between valid bounds, pointwise in J
